  "description": "A VT worker that dies while the core lives (F3d; C4 decision 4): the core restores the last snapshot into the restarted worker and feeds it the recording's own output frames past the commit point, then the frames recorded meanwhile; the data path never broke, so no C3 handshake runs. On this socket that is: the grid's close, the restarted worker's hello_ack reporting the grids it holds (empty — a fresh process, D19), and a restore of the snapshot at its snapshot_seq for each affected session, answered by restored with the same request_id. The re-feed of the recording's frames is graded by the U2 core (owed): this fixture invents no cross-socket machinery. That nothing is recorded twice is the recording side (C8), also U2 (owed). The U4 worker is owed.",
  "corpus": [
    "plan.md C4 decision 4",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json close",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json hello_ack",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json restore",
    "vt-ipc.schema.json restored"
  ],
  "case": {
    "socket": "vt-control",
